    ans: [
      "Organizes the enormous diversity of organisms into manageable groups.",
      "Makes identification of organisms easier.",
      "Provides standardized scientific names for communication.",
      "Helps scientists compare characteristics of organisms.",
      "Reveals similarities and evolutionary relationships.",
      "Supports research in biology and other life sciences.",
      "Helps scientists predict characteristics of organisms based on their groups.",
      "Assists in identifying and prioritizing species for conservation.",
      "Improves the study and documentation of biodiversity.",
      "Provides a common framework for sharing biological information internationally."
    ],
    why: "Classification creates an organized framework for studying biodiversity. By grouping organisms according to shared characteristics and evolutionary evidence, scientists can identify species, communicate accurately, investigate relationships and make informed conservation decisions."
