    why: "Energy flows through ecosystems rather than being recycled. Organisms use much of the energy they obtain for metabolism and other activities, and some energy remains in material that is not consumed or assimilated. Therefore, less energy is available to organisms at higher trophic levels, making the pyramid of energy upright."
