    ans: "Vegetative propagation can produce new plants quickly without requiring pollination or fertilization. It also produces plants that are usually genetically similar to the parent, helping preserve desirable characteristics.",
    why: "Asexual reproduction can allow rapid multiplication of organisms. In agriculture, vegetative propagation is useful for maintaining desirable characteristics such as fruit quality, although it can also reduce genetic variation."
