  {
    q: "A structure in the female reproductive system receives the penis during sexual intercourse and also forms the passage through which a baby passes during birth. Which structure performs both functions?",
    hint: "Think about the muscular canal connecting the cervix to the outside of the body.",
    steps: [
      "Identify the structure that receives the penis during intercourse.",
      "Identify the passage through which the baby is delivered.",
      "Determine whether the same structure performs both functions."
    ],
    ans: "The vagina receives the penis and semen during sexual intercourse and forms the birth canal through which the baby passes during delivery.",
    why: "The vagina is a muscular canal connecting the cervix to the outside of the body. It has roles in sexual intercourse and childbirth."
  }
